# 7. TYPOGRAPHY AND CONTENT SYSTEM

Review all visible text throughout the application.

Remove redundant headings, repeated explanations, technical jargon, and generic AI copy.

Use concise, human language.

Preferred language:

| Avoid | Use instead |
|---|---|
| Escrow protocol | Protected payment |
| Deploy escrow | Create payment agreement |
| Fund escrow | Add money |
| Beneficiary | Person receiving payment |
| Milestone | Work stage |
| Disbursement | Release payment |
| On-chain transaction | Payment record |
| Transaction hash | Transaction reference |
| Smart contract | Payment protection |
| Describe in plain words | What would you like to do? |

Do not force these replacements where they would make a particular screen confusing.

Keep technical information in existing advanced or transaction-detail areas where it is genuinely necessary.

Use a clear typographic system:
- Strong but restrained headings.
- Readable body text.
- Comfortable line height.
- Consistent font weights.
- No unnecessary uppercase labels.
- Avoid excessive bold text.

Every visible sentence should earn its place on the screen.

